# VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Pick the "local" environment (bottom-right),
# start infra + the four services, then click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Sign up (JSON API). The browser flow at /account/register works too.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "asha@example.com", "password": "Passw0rd!23", "name": "Asha Rao" }

### 2a. USER token via the dev-only password grant (Auth:EnablePasswordGrant=true in Development).
#      In production users sign in through the browser (authorization code + PKCE) - see the dashboard.
# @name userToken
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=asha@example.com&password=Passw0rd!23&scope=openid profile email booking payment status.read

###
@userJwt = {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 2b. Who am I? (token validated locally by auth-service)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}

### 3. Book a shipment (booking-service; scope "booking") -> writes shipment + outbox in ONE transaction
# @name booking
POST {{host}}/api/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "origin": "Delhi 110001", "destination": "Mumbai 400001", "receiverName": "Asha Rao", "weightKg": 2.5, "serviceLevel": "EXPRESS" }

###
@shipmentId = {{booking.response.body.$.id}}

### 4. Status (status-service). Within ~2 s the event arrives via Pub/Sub: BOOKED
GET {{host}}/api/status/shipments/{{shipmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}

### 5. Start a payment (payment-service; scope "payment"). Amount comes from booking-service, not from you.
# @name payment
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "shipmentId": "{{shipmentId}}" }

###
@paymentId = {{payment.response.body.$.paymentId}}

### 6. LOCAL ONLY (provider=fake): simulate the gateway reporting success (use outcome=failure to test failure)
POST {{host}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}/simulate?outcome=success
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}

### 7. Status is now CONFIRMED
GET {{host}}/api/status/shipments/{{shipmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}

### 8. MACHINE token (client_credentials): the carrier system. Secret = Seed:CarrierClientSecret (dev: dev-carrier-secret)
# @name carrierToken
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=carrier-sim&client_secret=dev-carrier-secret&scope=status.write

###
@carrierJwt = {{carrierToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 9. Carrier pushes delivery milestones: PICKED_UP -> IN_TRANSIT -> OUT_FOR_DELIVERY -> DELIVERED
POST {{host}}/api/status/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{carrierJwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "PICKED_UP", "note": "Collected from sender, Delhi hub" }

### 10. A USER token must NOT be able to do that (expect 403)
POST {{host}}/api/status/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{userJwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "DELIVERED" }

### OIDC discovery document and signing keys (what the APIs use to validate JWTs)
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

###
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks
